    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ageBand` derivation from an optional `birthDate`, keeping structural impact low by adding a small cohesive unit rather than growing any existing method.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`AgeBand.java` (new)** \u2014 a tiny, self-contained static helper (WMC_other = 0) computing the band from `birthDate` measured against `registrationDate`: `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+), and `null` when no birthDate. This mirrors the repo's existing `CheckDigit`/`IdentityKey` helper pattern.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (optional input date) to `OwnerFields` and `ageBand` (readOnly string) to `Owner`, so the generated DTOs carry the fields.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating `ageBand` to `AgeBand.of(owner)`. `birthDate` maps automatically by name, so no other method changed.\n\n4. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persisted `birthDate` field plus a trivial getter/setter (CC = 1 each).\n\n5. **hsqldb `schema.sql` / `data.sql`** \u2014 added the `birth_date` column and the matching value to the seed inserts (the hsqldb profile used by tests runs `ddl-auto=none`; I followed the existing precedent where only this schema tracks such columns, since h2 uses `ddl-auto=update`).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreDerivesAgeBand` and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
